    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d481">

                <pb facs="0607" n="505" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg505"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 13329/1–3.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt
                        to the Emperor of Japan.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic">May 1,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The American people are deeply grieved and shocked at the terrible naval disaster
                    which has just caused the loss of the lives of so many <pb facs="0608" n="506"
                        xml:id="pg506"/> gallant officers and men of the Japanese Navy. On their
                    behalf and personally on my own account I desire to express my profound sympathy
                    and concern, and I wish it were in my power to show this sympathy in more
                    practical fashion than by mere words.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Theodore
                    Roosevelt.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
